{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1SA",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the child Samuel ministered to the LORD before Eli. And the word of the LORD was precious in those days; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no open vision.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass at that time, when Eli ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " laid down in his place, and his eyes began to grow dim, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he could not see;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ere the lamp of God went out in the temple of the LORD, where the ark of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and Samuel was laid down ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to sleep",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the LORD called Samuel: and he answered, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he ran to Eli, and said, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I; for thou calledst me. And he said, I called not; lie down again. And he went and lay down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD called yet again, Samuel. And Samuel arose and went to Eli, and said, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I; for thou didst call me. And he answered, I called not, my son; lie down again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now Samuel did not yet know the LORD, neither was the word of the LORD yet revealed to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD called Samuel again the third time. And he arose and went to Eli, and said, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I; for thou didst call me. And Eli perceived that the LORD had called the child.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore Eli said to Samuel, Go, lie down: and it shall be, if he should call thee, that thou shalt say, Speak, LORD; for thy servant heareth. So Samuel went and lay down in his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD came, and stood and called as at other times, Samuel, Samuel. Then Samuel answered, Speak; for thy servant heareth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD said to Samuel, Behold, I will do a thing in Israel, at which both the ears of every one that heareth it shall tingle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that day I will perform against Eli all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which I have spoken concerning his house: when I begin, I will also make an end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I have told him, that I will judge his house for ever, for the iniquity which he knoweth: because his sons made themselves vile, and he restrained them not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And therefore I have sworn to the house of Eli, that the iniquity of Eli's house shall not be purged with sacrifice nor offering for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Samuel lay until the morning, and opened the doors of the house of the LORD: and Samuel feared to show Eli the vision.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Eli called Samuel, and said, Samuel, my son. And he answered, Here ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the thing that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the LORD",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath said to thee? I pray thee hide ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not from me: God do so to thee, and more also, if thou shalt hide ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thing from me, of all the things that he said to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Samuel told him every whit, and hid nothing from him. And he said, It ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD: let him do what seemeth him good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Samuel grew, and the LORD was with him, and let none of his words fall to the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all Israel, from Dan even to Beer-sheba, knew that Samuel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " established ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a prophet of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1SA.3.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1SA.3.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD appeared again in Shiloh: for the LORD revealed himself to Samuel in Shiloh by the word of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
